WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.320
Hello, and welcome to this setup walk through.

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:05.280
Right now we're going to cover building your constitution.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.800
So we're on step five.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.360
Your history is already searchable, and now we're going

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.480
to write the most important piece, your constitution.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.880
You know, it's not just a quick one page summary.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.600
It's actually an in-depth document, all about who you

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.840
are, how you work, and how to best work

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:22.240
with you, entirely written from your own words.

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:23.920
Your AI is going to read this document

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.160
at the start of every single conversation.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.400
Now, building this starts with questions.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.000
There are about 140 of them, broken down into sections.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.480
Things like who you are, your work, your

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:37.200
goals, and exactly how you use AI.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.360
It covers where you keep getting stuck, what

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.000
you prefer, and what you absolutely never want.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.480
We look at your values, your decisions, your

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.040
history, and even your life outside of work.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.760
It explores your strengths, your tradeoffs, how you

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.320
learn, what you need in different situations, what

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.640
should stay private, and the projects you've built.

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:56.320
And don't worry, if you don't run a

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:58.960
business, those business questions just simply stay empty.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:02.730
To do this, your conversations get sorted by length, from

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:06.570
mega and extra large down to large, medium, and small.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:09.130
Because those longest ones hold the most information

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:11.370
about you, the readers start right there.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:13.050
They only move down to your shorter

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.770
conversations if questions are still left unanswered.

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:17.610
That's really how the system gets such a

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.010
deep, accurate picture of you, without needing to

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:22.170
read every single chat you've ever had.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:25.290
So the readers answer each question using your exact

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:27.610
words, along with the date you said them.

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.250
Then a program comes in and checks every single

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:33.530
quote, word for word, against your actual conversations.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:36.570
If it doesn't match perfectly, it just gets thrown out.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.810
And keep in mind, text you pasted in

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:41.370
from somewhere else doesn't count as your voice.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:43.610
The things you actually said are kept totally

00:01:43.610 --> 00:01:46.330
separate from things the AI might have inferred.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:48.330
Plus, if nothing answers a specific

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:50.090
question, it just stays open.

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:52.730
Absolutely nothing gets made up about you.

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:56.250
Ultimately, each answer becomes a solid one to three paragraphs.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.280
They include specifics, how your thoughts might have changed

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.920
over time, and a real story pulled directly from

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.800
your own chats, with all the sources clearly listed.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.640
Now, this ends up being quite a long document.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:09.320
To put it into perspective, one real

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:11.800
example came out to around 60 pages.

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.440
Your AI will read through that entire document once

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:17.000
at the start of each and every conversation.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.600
You can actually see your specific

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.840
numbers right beside this setup explainer.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.920
It shows how many conversations are in each

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.480
size group, how many reading packets that creates,

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.320
and the estimated time it'll take.

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:29.560
This whole process runs on your AI plan's

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.400
allowance, and it goes a bit faster if

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.640
your tool can run several readers at once.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.240
While it works, you'll see a handy

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:37.320
countdown of the questions being answered.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:39.640
Once it's finally done, you'll be presented with

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:42.520
two short lists to review, things to confirm,

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:45.000
and any private details it might have found.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.120
If you spot anything that's wrong, just tell the system.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:51.400
And that specific part of the document is directly rewritten.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.960
You won't have to manage an ongoing list of corrections.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.760
The document itself just gets updated to be right.

00:02:57.070 --> 00:02:58.670
For your next step, the suggested

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:00.190
choice is Build It Now.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:01.630
You can just press a button below to get

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:06.110
started, Build It Now, Longest Conversations Only, or Later.
